   "text": "This is a cyclosporin A-type cyclic undecapeptide whose MeBmt side chain has been modified and linked to a lapatinib-like fragment. I read it in three parts.\n\n**Macrocycle.** Tracing the ring from the modified MeBmt residue, the sequence is MeBmt\u2013Abu\u2013Sar\u2013MeLeu\u2013Val\u2013MeLeu\u2013Ala\u2013D-Ala\u2013MeLeu\u2013MeLeu\u2013MeVal. This matches cyclosporin A, so I took its stereochemistry from the known cyclosporin A SMILES rather than reading each wedge individually. That stereo assignment is therefore not checked against the drawing.\n\n**Modified side chain.** In cyclosporin A the MeBmt side chain ends in CH2\u2013CH=CH\u2013CH3. Here it is CH(CH3)\u2013CH2CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013CH2\u2013, so the alkene is replaced by a saturated chain ending in an amide. That chain runs through an ethylenediamine linker to a furan at its 2-position.\n\n**Lapatinib-type fragment.** The furan's 5-position is bonded to C6 of a quinazoline. Quinazoline C4 carries an NH\u2013aryl group, where the aryl is 3-chloro-4-[(3-fluorobenzyl)oxy]phenyl.\n\nI did not recount every atom of the macrocycle against the image, so the final SMILES has not been verified atom for atom.\n\nSMILES: CC[C@H]1C(=O)N(CC(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N([C@H](C(=O)N1)[C@@H]([C@H](C)CCCC(=O)NCCNCc2ccc(o2)-c2ccc3ncnc(Nc4ccc(OCc5cccc(F)c5)c(Cl)c4)c3c2)O)C)C(C)C)C)CC(C)C)C)C)C)CC(C)C)C(C)C)CC(C)C)C)C"
